## Intuition
The core idea behind a palindrome is symmetry. If you look at the outermost characters of a word, they must be identical. If they are, you can mentally strip them away and look at the remaining inner characters. This naturally forms a recursive pattern: a string is a palindrome if its ends match and the remaining inside portion is also a palindrome.

